cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite the accompanying article and this repository."
title: "Data and code for: Barocaloric response of CrN: a large transition entropy behind a weak volume channel"
authors:
  - family-names: Rojas
    given-names: Tomas
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5745-4255"
    affiliation: "Universidad de Costa Rica"
  - family-names: Thorat
    given-names: Ruhi
    affiliation: "Ohio University"
abstract: >-
  Data and analysis code for a quasi-direct assessment of the barocaloric effect of CrN across its
  first-order antiferromagnetic magnetostructural transition, built entirely on published
  measurements. Includes the digitized specific heat, source-paired model inputs, Monte-Carlo
  uncertainty propagation, a blind validation on FeRh and Mn3NiN, a magnetic-field contrast, a
  Clausius-Clapeyron uniaxial-stress estimate, and a cross-material benchmark of barocaloric
  materials. Code: MIT; data: CC BY 4.0.
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24441835
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tomas0821/crn-barocaloric"
keywords:
  - barocaloric effect
  - CrN
  - magnetostructural transition
  - Clausius-Clapeyron
